From be53efeb4b19cac851d04dab8a57ed8a80b0b62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:51:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 336/371] pirates: "/code X" in chat answers "Code Redemption
 Failed" at once instead of nothing; nothing is sent outside (code-0001,
 UberDOG only)

Typing /code and a code showed "Redeeming Code X" and then nothing, forever. CodeRedemptionUD.sendCodeForRedemption
looked the sender up in the UberDOG's doId2do, where player avatars never are, so it returned at once. Past that it
called requestCodeVerification without its avatar argument (a TypeError) and posted the code to an outside site
(api.piratesclassic.com) whose answer handler is a TODO.

- No code server runs for the family game, so every code now answers status 0 to the sender at once
  (notifyClientCodeRedeemStatus -> the client's own CodeRedemptionBad line, "Code Redemption Failed"), through
  sendUpdateToAvatarId, the same reply path the friends manager uses. One UD info line per try. No sender avatar ->
  nothing sent. Nothing is posted outside.

UberDOG only; needs an UberDOG restart. No AI restart, no client publish. Test: test_code.py (stand-in UberDOG):
live FAIL (answered nothing), patched PASS 2/2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/coderedemption/CodeRedemptionUD.py | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pirates/coderedemption/CodeRedemptionUD.py b/pirates/coderedemption/CodeRedemptionUD.py
index e05a8e2..b6e8cb7 100644
--- a/pirates/coderedemption/CodeRedemptionUD.py
+++ b/pirates/coderedemption/CodeRedemptionUD.py
@@ -48,12 +48,15 @@ class CodeRedemptionUD(DistributedObjectGlobalUD):
             callback=handleVerifyCallback)
 
     def sendCodeForRedemption(self, code, username):
-        avatar = self.air.doId2do.get(self.air.getAvatarIdFromSender())
-        if not avatar:
+        # family server (11-20, code-0001): "/code X" in chat said "Redeeming Code X" and then nothing. Player avatars
+        # are not in the UberDOG's doId2do, so this returned at once; past that it called requestCodeVerification
+        # without its avatar and posted the code to an outside site whose answer is a TODO. No code server runs for
+        # the family game, so every code answers "failed" to the sender at once.
+        avatarId = self.air.getAvatarIdFromSender()
+        if not avatarId:
             return
-
-        code = code.lower()
-        self.requestCodeVerification(code, username)
+        self.notify.info('code redemption: avatar %s tried a code; no code server, answered failed' % avatarId)
+        self.d_notifyClientCodeRedeemStatus(avatarId, 0)
 
     def d_notifyClientCodeRedeemStatus(self, avatarId, status):
         self.notify.debug('Sending redeemp notify status (%s) to avatar (%s)' % (status, avatarId))
